  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "EncodePath percent-encodes every folder/model name. Fixes names containing #, ? or an existing %XX sequence (before, the request was cut off at #, ? started a query string and %XX was decoded by the server). All other reserved characters (&, +, ;, =, parentheses and others) are now escaped explicitly too; spaces and non-ASCII characters were already encoded and go over the wire as before. Behaviour of a real Revit Server with the escaped characters has not been verified yet. RenameFolderAsync escapes the new name. GetAllModelsRecursiveAsync throws instead of silently skipping a folder whose contents response is empty. RevitServerApiException and RevitServerUiApiException expose StatusCode and ResponseContent of HTTP error responses. Direct export: own WCF channel to /ModelService{year}/ (net.tcp, streamed) instead of Autodesk Proxy.dll, so the year is only a parameter; verified live against Revit Server 2022, 2023, 2024 and 2025 (docker test stand; the 2023-2025 servers served copies of 2022-format test models; BasicFileInfo in CreateLocal mode matched the official RevitServerTool 2022 and 2024 output); Revit Server 2026 and 2027 are expected to work by the same endpoint pattern but have not been verified against a live server. One bundled set of Autodesk client assemblies (Revit 2024) in RSAssemblies\\ instead of one folder per year, also included in dotnet publish output (kept as files with PublishSingleFile); the loader uses only a directory that directly contains the six DLLs (no recursive search; an AssembliesPath that does not qualify is skipped) and one set per process (InvalidOperationException otherwise, also when these assemblies are already loaded from another location); the server read lock is always released (UnlockData, retried like RevitServerTool; LockData Busy is retried too) and exports of the same model wait for each other (named mutex, as RevitServerTool); CancellationToken is honoured; the RVT is assembled in %TEMP% (about twice the model size is needed there) and replaces the destination file only when complete; new CreateLocal option writes the BasicFileInfo of a local copy like RevitServerTool; errors are exceptions with the operation, endpoint and model; the %TEMP%\\RevitServerNet_*.txt diagnostic files are no longer written; ExportModelAsync no longer puts the HTTP port into the net.tcp address; RevitVersion must be a four-digit year. See CHANGES.md.",
